WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.930
&gt;&gt; Good evening everyone.

00:00:05.931 --> 00:00:07.660
See, I would like to talk

00:00:07.661 --> 00:00:10.605
on Salaam Mumbai Foundation
and its program.

00:00:10.606 --> 00:00:12.690
Basically, my name
is Devak Patel,

00:00:12.691 --> 00:00:15.185
and I'm part of
Salaam Bombay Foundation.

00:00:15.186 --> 00:00:16.860
Salaam Mumbai Foundation is one

00:00:16.861 --> 00:00:19.030
of the branch of
Salaam Bombay Foundation.

00:00:19.031 --> 00:00:20.910
Salaam Bombay
Foundation basically

00:00:20.911 --> 00:00:23.220
work on tobacco control.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.320
So, Salaam Mumbai Foundation
which works in

00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:29.650
rural areas and
Salaam Bombay Foundation

00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:31.280
which works in urban areas.

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:33.525
So, basically,
Salaam Mumbai Foundation

00:00:33.526 --> 00:00:36.035
are raised in 2007 and

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.860
our prime motto objective is

00:00:37.861 --> 00:00:41.240
that making all schools
are tobacco-free,

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:46.010
and that's why we will engage
and train our trainers.

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:48.060
See basically at Maharashtra,

00:00:48.061 --> 00:00:51.050
we are working in all entire
districts of Maharashtra.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.355
There are 34 districts in

00:00:52.356 --> 00:00:54.710
Maharashtra, and
out of Marahashtra,

00:00:54.711 --> 00:00:56.285
we have replicated
these program in

00:00:56.286 --> 00:00:58.940
other state of India as
Rajasthan, Karnataka.

00:00:58.941 --> 00:01:02.070
We are Karnataka in Dharwad
and Havere districts,

00:01:02.071 --> 00:01:03.975
and Gujarat West Bengal.

00:01:03.976 --> 00:01:06.280
So, we are in
seven states of India,

00:01:06.281 --> 00:01:07.610
and basically in order to reach

00:01:07.611 --> 00:01:09.150
large numbers of children,

00:01:09.151 --> 00:01:12.210
and teachers direct, it's
very difficult to go

00:01:12.211 --> 00:01:15.440
and conduct negotiations
with the children, teachers.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.090
So, that's they will
develop different strategy,

00:01:18.091 --> 00:01:20.110
like we train the trainers.

00:01:20.111 --> 00:01:21.950
We train the trainers and once

00:01:21.951 --> 00:01:23.960
they get trained by our trainers,

00:01:23.961 --> 00:01:25.785
trained by Salaam
Mumbai foundation,

00:01:25.786 --> 00:01:28.170
then our trainers go

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:30.040
to their districts and
train other teachers.

00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:32.350
So, that is the strategy
we have develop.

00:01:32.351 --> 00:01:34.940
Then of course, we engage with

00:01:34.941 --> 00:01:38.140
ministry and the stakeholders
because at large level,

00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:39.580
we required permission from

00:01:39.581 --> 00:01:41.145
the government and
all these thing.

00:01:41.146 --> 00:01:42.470
So, that's why once they get

00:01:42.471 --> 00:01:44.765
motivated from
Salaam Mumbai Foundation,

00:01:44.766 --> 00:01:48.950
we get permission from
Education Department,

00:01:48.951 --> 00:01:53.090
and then we started implementing
program in the [inaudible] India.

00:01:53.091 --> 00:01:54.940
So basically, these
are the objectives in

00:01:54.941 --> 00:01:57.220
order to achieve
these objectives,

00:01:57.221 --> 00:02:01.830
we have replicated program
in different parts of India.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.275
So, as I said before that,

00:02:07.276 --> 00:02:10.770
it's very difficult to go and
meet each and every child,

00:02:10.771 --> 00:02:11.820
each and every trainers,

00:02:11.821 --> 00:02:15.130
teachers that's why we
develop different strategy.

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:16.170
We train the NGOs,

00:02:16.171 --> 00:02:18.850
we train our stakeholders,
like master trainer.

00:02:18.851 --> 00:02:22.040
So initially, we have started

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.540
programming in
Chandrapur districts

00:02:23.541 --> 00:02:25.230
in the eastern part
of Maharashtra,

00:02:25.231 --> 00:02:28.260
it's very remote areas
and tribal areas.

00:02:28.261 --> 00:02:30.940
Initially, we started
programming 10 villages,

00:02:30.941 --> 00:02:33.620
where we realize that
tobacco consumption rate is

00:02:33.621 --> 00:02:36.810
very high amongst the
male and female both,

00:02:36.811 --> 00:02:38.445
and adult and youth also.

00:02:38.446 --> 00:02:41.050
Initially, when we did
a survey in the 10 villages,

00:02:41.051 --> 00:02:44.600
we found that almost 45
villagers using tobacco.

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:47.635
I mean, all the tobacco
types are productive.

00:02:47.636 --> 00:02:48.950
It include superior also.

00:02:48.951 --> 00:02:50.240
So, what we feel is that

00:02:50.241 --> 00:02:54.185
[inaudible] are equally
harmful to the tobacco,

00:02:54.186 --> 00:02:57.130
because in Maharashtra
sweet tobacco

00:02:57.131 --> 00:02:58.960
is banned by the
government not by NGOs.

00:02:58.961 --> 00:03:00.370
It is band by government,

00:03:00.371 --> 00:03:02.120
but it's not properly implemented

00:03:02.121 --> 00:03:04.330
by Enforcement Agency,
that is different part.

00:03:04.331 --> 00:03:07.430
But it's banned by the
government in Maharashtra.

00:03:07.431 --> 00:03:10.365
Then, gradually we feel

00:03:10.366 --> 00:03:14.200
that it's a burning issue
not only in small districts,

00:03:14.201 --> 00:03:15.320
burning issue in all over

00:03:15.321 --> 00:03:17.335
the Maharashtra
because as of now,

00:03:17.336 --> 00:03:20.560
if the GATS data
says that almost in

00:03:20.561 --> 00:03:24.090
Maharashtra 26 percent adult
use tobacco in Maharashtra.

00:03:24.091 --> 00:03:26.540
If you think about
the India level,

00:03:26.541 --> 00:03:30.570
29 percent rate, tobacco
consumption rates in India.

00:03:30.571 --> 00:03:32.120
So, that's why we

00:03:32.121 --> 00:03:34.540
started implementing
program Maharashtra gradually,

00:03:34.541 --> 00:03:36.120
expanded program in Maharashtra.

00:03:36.121 --> 00:03:37.250
As of now, we have covered

00:03:37.251 --> 00:03:38.750
all the districts of Maharashtra.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.390
We directly go each and
in every districts,

00:03:41.391 --> 00:03:42.625
we train the teachers.

00:03:42.626 --> 00:03:43.835
We have develop lot of

00:03:43.836 --> 00:03:46.220
digitized material
and hard copies,

00:03:46.221 --> 00:03:47.860
and all these thing,
and based on that,

00:03:47.861 --> 00:03:49.790
the teachers and NGOs

00:03:49.791 --> 00:03:52.140
started implementing
this program as their own,

00:03:52.141 --> 00:03:55.365
in the schools and community.

00:03:55.366 --> 00:03:58.550
So, in 2014 in Ralgad district,

00:03:58.551 --> 00:03:59.680
there is a Mhasala block,

00:03:59.681 --> 00:04:02.360
and there are around 136.

00:04:02.361 --> 00:04:06.040
Schools are there right from
first two to As standards.

00:04:06.041 --> 00:04:08.605
So, all these schools have
become now tobacco free.

00:04:08.606 --> 00:04:12.740
We have kind of evidence
that all these schools,

00:04:12.741 --> 00:04:14.840
now if you go and meet
the teachers you will

00:04:14.841 --> 00:04:17.830
find that no one teachers
are consuming tobacco.

00:04:17.831 --> 00:04:19.820
I mean, how can we say

00:04:19.821 --> 00:04:21.490
that these schools
are tobacco free?

00:04:21.491 --> 00:04:25.630
There are criteria
developed by CBC board,

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.230
and based on that criteria,

00:04:27.231 --> 00:04:29.225
we declare that these schools

00:04:29.226 --> 00:04:31.955
now has become
a tobacco free schools.

00:04:31.956 --> 00:04:33.620
These are the criteria.

00:04:33.621 --> 00:04:37.030
Follow that criteria
each and every level.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:42.110
In 2015, we conducted

00:04:42.111 --> 00:04:47.250
a pledge activity in
Yavatmal across districts.

00:04:47.251 --> 00:04:50.730
Then that pledge registering
Limca book of records,

00:04:50.731 --> 00:04:55.830
and we also got
some Vysaanmukti Award

00:04:55.831 --> 00:04:57.725
from Maharashtra
government because of

00:04:57.726 --> 00:05:01.945
no greater work on tobacco
control at India level.

00:05:01.946 --> 00:05:07.950
Now, what we feel that there
is some kind of limitations.

00:05:07.951 --> 00:05:10.535
As a NGO, we're talking
with teachers like,

00:05:10.536 --> 00:05:13.505
talk on effects of tobacco,

00:05:13.506 --> 00:05:15.545
tobacco free schools etc.

00:05:15.546 --> 00:05:17.510
So, our real issue it was not to

00:05:17.511 --> 00:05:19.430
become a mandatory
to the teachers.

00:05:19.431 --> 00:05:21.460
Like they were saying
it's the NGOs agenda.

00:05:21.461 --> 00:05:22.520
It's not our agenda.

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:25.185
How can you say that
you talk on tobacco,

00:05:25.186 --> 00:05:28.145
effects of tobacco and
tobacco free schools.

00:05:28.146 --> 00:05:29.840
But now we made

00:05:29.841 --> 00:05:32.505
timed up adequacy with
the government, and law.

00:05:32.506 --> 00:05:36.065
In 2015, government
got convinced,

00:05:36.066 --> 00:05:38.885
and they integrated like
anti-tobacco messages

00:05:38.886 --> 00:05:40.840
in school curriculum,
in Maharashtra.

00:05:40.841 --> 00:05:42.330
I'm talking about Maharashtra,

00:05:42.331 --> 00:05:44.560
and in there stand also

00:05:44.561 --> 00:05:47.555
they're integrity
anti-tobacco message they see.

00:05:47.556 --> 00:05:50.760
Government in Maharashtra,
government has also developed

00:05:50.761 --> 00:05:53.210
kind of like
government's software,

00:05:53.211 --> 00:05:56.700
where we integrated that
all 11 criteria in their system.

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:59.540
So, that now it's become a
mandatory to all the teachers,

00:05:59.541 --> 00:06:02.460
like they have to enter

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:06.530
all the tobacco-free school
data in that system.

00:06:06.531 --> 00:06:09.905
So in 2017, we succeeded on that,

00:06:09.906 --> 00:06:11.720
and also this is all

00:06:11.721 --> 00:06:13.430
are done of Salaam
Mumbai Foundation.

00:06:13.431 --> 00:06:15.755
We initially started
program 2007.

00:06:15.756 --> 00:06:20.280
Now, we are in say
one state of, as of now,

00:06:20.281 --> 00:06:25.635
we train around 80,000
teachers at seven states,

00:06:25.636 --> 00:06:28.904
and now around 4,000

00:06:28.905 --> 00:06:31.810
have become tobacco free in
the state of Maharashtra.

00:06:31.811 --> 00:06:35.875
So, that is the milestone of
Salaam Mumbai Foundation.

00:06:35.876 --> 00:06:44.490
Next. So, we have developed
like digitized material.

00:06:44.491 --> 00:06:45.540
So as of now,

00:06:45.541 --> 00:06:48.540
we have different kind of
films and all these thing.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.020
We have developed
Tobacco Free School app.

00:06:51.021 --> 00:06:53.450
Once you type on
Google Play store,

00:06:53.451 --> 00:06:55.080
the app will come on practice,

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.710
and then teachers and NGOs can

00:06:57.711 --> 00:07:01.805
easily enter the data in
that Tobacco Free School app.

00:07:01.806 --> 00:07:04.475
So, we get all the evidence.

00:07:04.476 --> 00:07:06.755
Before two months back,

00:07:06.756 --> 00:07:09.320
we declared an
underbar districts in

00:07:09.321 --> 00:07:12.735
Maharashtra that these districts
are tobacco free.

00:07:12.736 --> 00:07:13.990
This is why we declared

00:07:13.991 --> 00:07:16.170
their district because we
have kind of evidence.

00:07:16.171 --> 00:07:17.920
No one can challenge that.

00:07:17.921 --> 00:07:20.980
How can you declare
these district?

00:07:20.981 --> 00:07:24.200
The important thing
is that as an NGO,

00:07:24.201 --> 00:07:26.065
we don't have that kind of power.

00:07:26.066 --> 00:07:31.730
That we can declare the district
is tobacco free No.

00:07:31.731 --> 00:07:35.090
So, we convince magistrate
that see we have like

00:07:35.091 --> 00:07:38.995
one 1,400 evidence received
from the teachers,

00:07:38.996 --> 00:07:40.310
and based on that, you can

00:07:40.311 --> 00:07:42.140
declare that this is our received

00:07:42.141 --> 00:07:43.335
and all schools have become a

00:07:43.336 --> 00:07:45.310
tobacco free, and then we start

00:07:45.311 --> 00:07:47.920
Mallinath Kalshetti is
the district magistrate

00:07:47.921 --> 00:07:50.235
of Nandurbar district.

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:52.800
He declared that our districts,

00:07:52.801 --> 00:07:56.285
all schools are
tobacco-free districts.

00:07:56.286 --> 00:07:59.525
Now, this year,
[inaudible] dream of

00:07:59.526 --> 00:08:01.140
Salaam Mumbai
Foundation that we are

00:08:01.141 --> 00:08:02.890
expecting that in Maharashtra,

00:08:02.891 --> 00:08:04.080
there around one lakh

00:08:04.081 --> 00:08:06.210
nine thousand schools
in Maharashtra,

00:08:06.211 --> 00:08:07.305
and we're expecting that

00:08:07.306 --> 00:08:09.200
all schools should
be tobacco-free.

00:08:09.201 --> 00:08:11.755
But how can we make that
schools tobacco-free

00:08:11.756 --> 00:08:15.210
unless we get data
from the teachers?

00:08:15.211 --> 00:08:18.050
We'll talk on the barriers of

00:08:18.051 --> 00:08:20.675
the Tobacco Free School app.

00:08:20.676 --> 00:08:23.699
Now, we have developed Salaam
Mumbai Foundation websites

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:27.140
where we have uploaded
all the films, stories,

00:08:27.141 --> 00:08:30.445
booklets, and lot of
best stories, success stories,

00:08:30.446 --> 00:08:31.810
government GRs,

00:08:31.811 --> 00:08:34.685
notification, FDI
notification, et cetera.

00:08:34.686 --> 00:08:36.460
So, we've also Salaam

00:08:36.461 --> 00:08:38.270
Mumbai Foundation
Facebook page developed,

00:08:38.271 --> 00:08:40.370
Learning Management System
like any one.

00:08:40.371 --> 00:08:43.125
Now, this Learning Management
System is a system,

00:08:43.126 --> 00:08:47.009
is a kind of website,

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.900
if you want to learn

00:08:48.901 --> 00:08:51.200
something about
Tobacco Control Program.

00:08:51.201 --> 00:08:53.850
Once you complete that course,

00:08:53.851 --> 00:08:55.805
you will get certificate online.

00:08:55.806 --> 00:08:57.555
So, that system will come in

00:08:57.556 --> 00:08:59.825
practice after
maybe one or two months.

00:08:59.826 --> 00:09:01.065
So, it will help to

00:09:01.066 --> 00:09:03.895
strengthen program at
village and school level.

00:09:03.896 --> 00:09:07.310
So, that is overall about
digitized material, and really,

00:09:07.311 --> 00:09:10.005
I can say that
the digitized material help

00:09:10.006 --> 00:09:13.710
us to strengthen program at
school and community level.

00:09:13.711 --> 00:09:16.560
&gt;&gt; I think the challenge
that these guys are facing,

00:09:16.561 --> 00:09:17.975
and I'm interjecting here,

00:09:17.976 --> 00:09:19.300
is that they have

00:09:19.301 --> 00:09:21.595
enough digital information
available to them,

00:09:21.596 --> 00:09:24.265
but it's stand alone
and it's static.

00:09:24.266 --> 00:09:27.710
It does not have
any intelligence in it.

00:09:27.711 --> 00:09:30.520
They've not been able to do
any predictive analysis,

00:09:30.521 --> 00:09:32.290
nor have they been able to

00:09:32.291 --> 00:09:34.130
do some prescriptive
analysis which could

00:09:34.131 --> 00:09:37.900
be further used as
influencing mechanisms.

00:09:37.901 --> 00:09:42.340
So, the opportunity lies
here is that there is a mine

00:09:42.341 --> 00:09:44.150
of digital data that's already in

00:09:44.151 --> 00:09:47.225
place across all Maharashtra,

00:09:47.226 --> 00:09:49.655
and that's a significant
amount of data set.

00:09:49.656 --> 00:09:53.085
If that can be put
through an engine which

00:09:53.086 --> 00:09:56.670
can provide some intelligence
around it, it will, a,

00:09:56.671 --> 00:09:59.825
give us better decision
making, second,

00:09:59.826 --> 00:10:02.390
lot of their process is
today manual in nature,

00:10:02.391 --> 00:10:03.840
in terms of data collection and

00:10:03.841 --> 00:10:05.450
in terms of other aspects.

00:10:05.451 --> 00:10:07.205
So, how can that be digitized?

00:10:07.206 --> 00:10:09.345
So, that's the
opportunity statement out

00:10:09.346 --> 00:10:12.145
here that we have from the team.

00:10:12.146 --> 00:10:16.975
So, open to any
questions you have.

00:10:16.976 --> 00:10:18.395
&gt;&gt; Yeah, please.

00:10:18.396 --> 00:10:21.985
&gt;&gt; So, this is
a very big success story.

00:10:21.986 --> 00:10:23.730
Congratulations. My question is,

00:10:23.731 --> 00:10:27.170
what kind of data do you
have on the basis of

00:10:27.171 --> 00:10:31.095
which we can make some kind
of predictive analytics?

00:10:31.096 --> 00:10:33.000
For example, data on

00:10:33.001 --> 00:10:37.140
individual students
or class level

00:10:37.141 --> 00:10:40.175
so that we can make
some predictions about,

00:10:40.176 --> 00:10:42.965
this student is not
going to become

00:10:42.966 --> 00:10:45.235
tobacco-free or this student
will become tobacco-free,

00:10:45.236 --> 00:10:48.030
or something on the basis
of which we can say,

00:10:48.031 --> 00:10:49.785
this student needs
more intervention

00:10:49.786 --> 00:10:51.870
and this student does
not need intervention,

00:10:51.871 --> 00:10:54.120
so that we can do

00:10:54.121 --> 00:10:56.415
something of that type with
respect to prescription.

00:10:56.416 --> 00:10:57.600
So, I wanted to get some

00:10:57.601 --> 00:10:58.880
idea of what you're
thinking about.

00:10:58.881 --> 00:11:02.510
&gt;&gt; So, we have collected
school-wise data.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:06.060
We don't have individual
data at present,

00:11:06.061 --> 00:11:07.680
but it's a really good idea.

00:11:07.681 --> 00:11:09.920
But now, this is our learning.

00:11:09.921 --> 00:11:16.625
Now, just we've replicated
program in Uttar Pradesh.

00:11:16.626 --> 00:11:18.125
District name is Pratapgarh.

00:11:18.126 --> 00:11:19.965
So, there, we have done

00:11:19.966 --> 00:11:22.400
baseline survey with
the children and teachers.

00:11:22.401 --> 00:11:24.580
But in Maharashtra, we don't have

00:11:24.581 --> 00:11:27.950
that kind of
baseline survey data.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:31.685
&gt;&gt; So, the basic concept is,

00:11:31.686 --> 00:11:35.155
if the children are kept far from

00:11:35.156 --> 00:11:40.835
tobacco and other harmful things
up to the age of 18,

00:11:40.836 --> 00:11:43.504
then it's very likely

00:11:43.505 --> 00:11:48.350
he will stay away for
the rest of the life.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.585
It's very difficult.
The Maharashtra state

00:11:51.586 --> 00:11:57.955
has one [inaudible] nine
thousand schools itself,

00:11:57.956 --> 00:12:01.500
and it's very difficult to
reach each individual student.

00:12:01.501 --> 00:12:05.970
As an NGO, we don't have
that much capacity.

00:12:05.971 --> 00:12:10.180
So, the design was to
work with the schools.

00:12:10.181 --> 00:12:13.280
We have law, we have guidelines
from the CBSE board.

00:12:13.281 --> 00:12:17.950
So, if we could make
schools tobacco-free,

00:12:17.951 --> 00:12:21.040
then the children
don't have access

00:12:21.041 --> 00:12:24.805
or they're not exposed to
this kind of substance.

00:12:24.806 --> 00:12:28.565
It's likely to impact
their life positively.

00:12:28.566 --> 00:12:30.565
So, idea was that.
So, we have data.

00:12:30.566 --> 00:12:31.970
Like we have schools,

00:12:31.971 --> 00:12:33.310
